    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[FF144 CSSStyleProperties CSS2Properties]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27975</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27975"/>
        <updated>2025-09-28T23:15:13.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF144 added support for <code class="notranslate">CSSStyleProperties</code> in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1919582" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1919582</a> , as updated in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3422725499" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27902" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27902/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27902">#27902</a></p>
<p dir="auto">However as explained in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1919582#c30" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1919582#c30</a> the  <code class="notranslate">CSSStyleProperties</code> was renamed from a preexisting <code class="notranslate">CSS2Properties</code>. This adds the alternative name to the feature for Firefox. Note that the developer indicates this was from version 2 (checked) but might have been version 1.</p>
<p dir="auto">FF145 added support for returning this from <code class="notranslate">.style</code> in elements (HTML, SVG, MathML) and also in <code class="notranslate">getComputedStyle()</code> in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1989925" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1989925</a>. I have set these to have a subfeature indicating the new return type.</p>
<p dir="auto">It is not clear if FF returns it from <code class="notranslate">CSSStyleRule.style</code> - I am asking in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1989925#c4" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1989925#c4</a></p>
<p dir="auto">Chrome hasn't added support for <code class="notranslate">CSSStyleProperties</code> as far as I can tell.</p>
<p dir="auto">Safari has been marked as supporting  <code class="notranslate">CSSStyleProperties</code> in 26 already, but the return methods were not marked. I have set all of them to working in that version though I have not tested it (they appear to be updated in source though, and 26 was the version the interface went in).</p>
<p dir="auto">In addition, the spec changed to move the <code class="notranslate">cssFloat</code> attribute from <code class="notranslate">CSSStyleDeclaration</code> to <code class="notranslate">CSSStyleProperties</code>. This won't affect FF which never implemented that, but it does affect Safari. So I've marked it as removed and also now non-standard and deprecated.</p>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3417388824" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41133" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/41133/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41133">mdn/content#41133</a></p>]]></content>
        <author>
            <name>hamishwillee</name>
            <email>hamishwillee@noreply.github.com</email>
            <uri>https://github.com/hamishwillee</uri>
        </author>
        <published>2025-09-23T05:28:06.000Z</published>
    </entry>
    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[FF144 cross-origin iframe requires user interaction for top-navigation]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27960</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27960"/>
        <updated>2025-09-30T13:20:03.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF144 adds support for cross-origin <code class="notranslate">&lt;iframe&gt;</code> to require sticky activation and user permission before it can do <code class="notranslate">Window.top</code> navigation (i.e. set <code class="notranslate">top.location</code>) in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1419501" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1419501</a></p>
<p dir="auto">This was originally supported in Chrome 68 (<a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5851021045661696" rel="nofollow">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5851021045661696</a>) and Safari 13 (<a href="https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=193076" rel="nofollow">https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=193076</a>).</p>
<p dir="auto">Note that this is not standard though AFAIK. There are discussions in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="1272422076" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8013" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/whatwg/html/issues/8013/hovercard" href="https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8013">whatwg/html#8013</a> and all the main browsers comply, but no place to point in the HTML spec. Further there are tests, but these aren't all passed by anyone and are marked as experimental.</p>
<p dir="auto">Note that according to <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1419501#c28" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1419501#c28</a> if the redirect is blocked then Chrome and FF will prompt for user permission to navigate and log the error in console, while Safari just blocks the navigation and reports and error in the dev console.</p>
<p dir="auto">Related work can be tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3417409664" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41138" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/41138/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41138">mdn/content#41138</a></p>]]></content>
        <author>
            <name>hamishwillee</name>
            <email>hamishwillee@noreply.github.com</email>
            <uri>https://github.com/hamishwillee</uri>
        </author>
        <published>2025-09-22T03:22:40.000Z</published>
    </entry>
